            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            on ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            between them. These are the “abstract coordinate charts” from the discussion at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets"} geometry of physics – smooth sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SuperCartSp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SuperCartSp
            as
            %strong abstract super coordinate systems
            and to develop a geometry induced from these.
          %p
            Recall the two magic algebraic properties of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            that make the above algebraic description of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            work:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                (
                %strong>
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds+into+formal+duals+of+R-algebras"} embedding of smooth manifolds into formal duals of R-algebras
                ) The functor that assigns
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebras of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi SmthMfd
                      %mo ↪
                      %msubsup
                        %mi CAlg
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi op
